{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"defectible-befuddling-sheldrake","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`pytest-split==0.11.0` is pinned (`pyproject.toml:274`) but `.test_durations` is git-ignored as \"never committed\" (`.gitignore:65-66`, task 9ad9); no duration profile exists for splitting the suite, nor for the AGENTS.md 20-25 minute `make verify` budget. This story runs last in the epic so the profile covers the final suite after S1-S4. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\n- Remove `.gitignore:65-66`.\n- Run once from the repo root: `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal --store-durations --clean-durations -q -p no:cacheprovider`. pytest-split writes on the controller's `pytest_sessionfinish` from `terminalreporter.stats` (`pytest_split/plugin.py:188-227`), so the xdist workers' reports are included.\n- Commit `.test_durations` (sorted JSON, ~2 MB for ~19.2k nodes).\n- Add `\\.test_durations` to the `check-added-large-files` `exclude` at `.pre-commit-config.yaml:33`, making it `^(uv\\.lock|\\.test_durations)$` (the 500 KB default cap would reject the file).\n- Add `### Per-test durations (.test_durations)` under `docs/local-dev-env.md:462` \"Day-to-day gates\" (after `:528`): the command above, that the file is refreshed by a deliberate re-run only, and `pytest --splits N --group K` usage.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `.gitignore`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, `.test_durations` (new), `docs/local-dev-env.md`. Out of scope: any CI workflow change that consumes the profile (`--splits`/`--group` is not wired into CI here), `pyproject.toml`, the `Makefile`, and every test module.\n\n## Testing\n`python -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('.test_durations'));print(len(d))\"` equals the node count printed by `pytest --collect-only -q -m \"not integration and not external\" | tail -1`; `pre-commit run --all-files` green; `pytest --splits 4 --group 1 --collect-only -q` collects a quarter of the suite; `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` green; the key count, the collect count and the group-1 count are recorded on this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.test_durations` is tracked (`git ls-files .test_durations` prints it) and its key count equals the default-selection node count (the two commands above, recorded on this ticket).\n- [ ] `pre-commit run --all-files` accepts the file (`check-added-large-files` passes with the extended `exclude`).\n- [ ] The `### Per-test durations (.test_durations)` section exists in `docs/local-dev-env.md` and `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` passes.\n- [ ] `pytest --splits 4 --group 1 --collect-only -q` collects a quarter of the suite (count recorded on this ticket).\n- [ ] `make verify` green.","id":"e873-b770-693c-4ff5","parent_id":"f400-65b3-1899-4af9","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Record per-test durations once and commit .test_durations for pytest-split"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807220524870893,"uuid":"63d4dbae-26c2-49f7-abd0-5bb3e95b5c82"}